Well, "better" is tricky, since we never tested =A0how "good" the Loglan/Lo=
jban system was. =A0But a priori creations would help with issues that the =
present system ignores, like better word separation (the noisy channel prob=
lem or just finding more rafsi) or more equitable phoneme distribution (for=
 some aesthetic reason). =A0But it is a real pain to do, whereas the presen=
t system gave a good starting point that got the creators most of the way t=
hrough the list. =A0Of course, a program could be devised to generate a fie=
ld of =A0words of predetermined form, satisfying the distribution criteria =
and then assign them willy-nilly (or even under some criteria) to a list (f=
rom somewhere -- maybe Loglan, after all) of meanings. I'm not sure that wo=
uld be significantly harder to learn the the gismu list (and, indeed, it mi=
ght well provide a real test for the claim that the present list is easy to=
 learn -- against everyone's experiences).


